[Context: Cours Programme 2026/2027 > Semestre 1 > **UE AI Game Programming (EN)** - 3 ECTS]
# Cours Programme 2026/2027  
## Semestre 1  
### **UE AI Game Programming (EN)** - 3 ECTS  
- Lecteur: M. Regin
- This course presents different techniques to program games for one or two players. For two-player games, only full information games will be considered.
- The students will have to develop, in groups of two, a program that will simulate a human player.
A competition between the programs will be organized and it will determine the notes.

---

[Context: Cours Programme 2026/2027 > Semestre 2 > **UE Combinatorial Optimization** (EN) - 3 ECTS]
### **UE Combinatorial Optimization** (EN) - 3 ECTS  
- Lecteur: M. Regin
- This course presents greedy algorithms, decision diagrams, and markov models.

---

[Context: Cours Programme 2026/2027 > Semestre 1 > **UE Software Engineering Software engineering and Design patterns**(EN) - 3 ECTS]
### **UE Software Engineering Software engineering and Design patterns**(EN) - 3 ECTS  
- Lecteur: Leturc, Regin

---

[Context: Cours Programme 2026/2027 > Semestre 2 > **UE Modélisation par des contraintes**- 3 ECTS]
### **UE Modélisation par des contraintes**- 3 ECTS  
- Lecteur: M. Malapert
- Les principes fondamentaux de la programmation linéaire et de la programmation par contraintes sont abordés en vue d’une meilleure exploitation des ces méthodes. La programmation linéaire est une technique largement utilisée pour résoudre des problèmes d’optimisation linéaire. Quant à la programmation par contraintes, elle s’avère particulièrement adaptée à la résolution de problèmes combinatoires complexes, comme ceux liés à l’ordonnancement ou à la planification.
- L’objectif principal du cours est l’apprentissage de la modélisation de ces problèmes que ce soit en programmation linéaire ou en programmation par contraintes. Nous adoptons une approche comparative empirique pour déterminer quelle méthode est la plus adaptée pour un problème particulier.

---

[Context: Cours Programme 2026/2027 > Semestre 1 > **UE Model Checking for AI** (EN) - 3 ECTS]
### **UE Model Checking for AI** (EN) - 3 ECTS  
- Lecteur: Mme. De Maria
- This course covers methods and tools for automatically checking
whether a system (software or hardware) meets a given specification.
- Course program
- The need for formal methods to verify hardware and software systems
- Reactive systems
- The model-checking process and its advantages
- System modeling (Kripke structure)
- Specification modeling (CTL and LTL temporal logics, fairness)
- Model-checking algorithms and their complexity
- Improvements: symbolic model-checking and on-the-fly model-checking
- Realistic examples

---

[Context: Cours Programme 2026/2027 > Semestre 2 > **UE Logic for AI** (EN) - 3 ECTS]
### **UE Logic for AI** (EN) - 3 ECTS  
- Lecteur: M. Tettamanzi
- The objective of this course is to provide a general background in Logic to enable access to more advanced topics in computer science and, more specifically, in artificial intelligence. Intelligent systems in the real world have to deal with issues like uncertainty, imprecision, and incompleteness. Some prominent logical tools that can be used to approach these issues are thus discussed.
- **Lectures**
- Part I. Basics
- Propositional Logic: syntax and semantics
- First Order Predicate Logic: syntax and semantics
- Natural Deduction
- Unification and Resolution
- Part II. Non-Monotonic Logic and Approximate Reasoning
- Argumentation Theory
- Belief Revision and Update
- Fuzzy Logic
- Possibility Theory

---

[Context: Cours Programme 2026/2027 > Semestre 2 > **UE Introduction to Multiagent Systems** (EN) - 3 ECTS]
### **UE Introduction to Multiagent Systems** (EN) - 3 ECTS  
- Lecteur: M. Leturc
- This course provides an introduction to the fundamental concepts, models, and applications of Multi-Agent Systems (MAS).
Students will learn how autonomous agents interact, cooperate, and compete within distributed environments. Topics include the taxonomy and architectures of MAS, coordination and communication mechanisms, decision-making under uncertainty, and social dynamics such as voting, reputation, and argumentation. The course also introduces elements of planning, game theory, and computational social choice theory, bridging theoretical models of MAS with practical applications.

---

[Context: Cours Programme 2026/2027 > Semestre 1 > **UE AI: Models and Applications** (EN) - 3 ECTS]
### **UE AI: Models and Applications** (EN) - 3 ECTS  
- Lecteur: M. Enrico
- The main goal of the course is to introduce the students to the different concepts of machine learning by neural networks (also several other models will be considered). For most subjects, first the formal aspects and concepts will be introduced and explained, then they will be illustrated through a series of programming exercises and experiments.
- [https://upinfo.univ-cotedazur.fr/s1/AI-models/](https://upinfo.univ-cotedazur.fr/s1/AI-models/)

